    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "How to start"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "**Find this year's dates and rules** on the organiser's own page. Dates change every year."
        },
        {
          "text": "**Work through past problems.** Olympiad problems are different from school exams, and past problems are the best preparation. Ask the organiser or older participants where to find them."
        },
        {
          "text": "**Go to every round you reach,** even if you do not expect to win. Camps and later rounds teach the most."
        },
        {
          "text": "**Keep a record** of each round you reach, with dates, for your applications."
        }
      ],
      "ordered": true
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Beyond olympiads"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "**Hackathons:** the NASA Space Apps Challenge is held in several cities in Bangladesh.",
          "cite": [
            "bd/competition.spaceApps"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Science fairs and project competitions:** school, district and national fairs let you show something you built or found."
        },
        {
          "text": "**Debate and Model United Nations:** your school's club is the place to start."
        },
        {
          "text": "**Writing and essay competitions:** good practice for the essays your applications need."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "No single competition decides an application. Universities look at what you did over years, and why.",
      "link": "profile"
    }
  ]
